          "text": "# Standard Repository Pattern: Data Requirement to Estimate TE\n\nThis document defines the standardized implementation pattern for tax-specific data repositories in the Tax-ETS system (Profit Tax, VAT, Salary Tax, etc.). This pattern ensures data precision through dictionary mapping while supporting both batch Excel imports and manual data entry.\n\n## 1. The Precision Pipeline (Import)\nTo ensure high-quality data, the import process must normalize incoming Excel data against the system's Data Dictionary.\n\n### Smart Mapping Logic\nWhen importing from Excel, the system should not trust plain text. It must attempt to \"snap\" text to the nearest dictionary entry:\n- **Normalization**: Trim whitespace and convert to uppercase for comparison.\n- **Matching**: Compare against the `province`, `district`, and `business_sectors` tables.\n- **Preservation**: If no match is found, preserve the original text but flag it in the UI (Layer 3).\n\n```php\n// Example Implementation in import_[tax_type].php\n$normalize = function($text, $choices) {\n    $text = strtoupper(trim($text));\n    foreach ($choices as $choice) {\n        if (strtoupper($choice) === $text) return $choice; // Snap to Dictionary\n    }\n    return $text; // Keep original for manual correction\n};\n```\n\n## 2. Integrated Management (View, Add, Edit)\nEvery data requirement page must support a unified interface for viewing and managing records.\n\n### Unified Modal Editor\nUse a single Bootstrap modal to handle both **Add** and **Edit** actions.\n- **Add Record**: Resets the form and sets `action = add_company`.\n- **Edit Record**: Pre-fills the form from a JSON data object and sets `action = update_company`.\n\n### Dictionary-Driven Dropdowns\nText inputs for geographic and sectoral data are forbidden. Use `<select>` elements:\n- **Province**: Populated from the `province` table.\n- **District**: Filtered dynamically via JavaScript when a province is selected.\n- **Sector**: Populated from the `business_sectors` table.\n\n## 3. The Shortcut Workflow (Calculate)\nThe \"Calculation\" button within the repository view acts as a contextual shortcut.\n- It must redirect to the central `calculator.php` or `te_[tax_type].php`.\n- It must pass the `batch_id` as a GET parameter to automatically pre-select the relevant data for the user.\n\n---\n\n## 4. Implementation Checklist for New Tax Types\n1. [ ] **Database**: Ensure the table has an `import_batch_id` column.\n2. [ ] **Import**: Implement the \"Smart Mapping\" logic in the PHP import script.\n3. [ ] **UI Header**: Add a \"Record Count\", \"Add Record\" button, and \"Run TE Calculation\" button.\n4. [ ] **Data Table**: Include an \"Action\" column with an Edit button.\n5. [ ] **Modal**: Implement a large (`modal-xl`) modal with dictionary selects and chained district filtering.\n6. [ ] **Sync**: Ensure all changes are synchronized to the web root."
