e dictionary standards through the UI.\n\n### ID-Based Dropdowns\nAll selection inputs must use the **ID** as the `value`. \n- **Chained Filtering**: The District dropdown must filter based on the `pro_id` for absolute precision.\n- **Auto-Sync**: When a record is saved manually via ID, the system must automatically fetch the corresponding Name from the dictionary to keep the dual-columns synchronized.\n\n### Unified Modal Editor\nUse a single `modal-xl` Bootstrap modal to handle both **Add** and **Edit** actions. Reset the form and change the `action` hidden field based on the user's intent.\n\n## 4. Post-Import Validation UI\nThe record list view (`view_companies.php`) should visually flag data inconsistencies:\n- **Missing IDs**: Highlight any row where `pro_id` or `sector_id` is `NULL` with a warning icon (⚠️).\n- **Direct Correction**: The \"Edit\" button allows the user to immediately fix unmapped data by selecting a valid entry from the dictionary dropdowns.\n\n---\n\n## 5. Implementation Checklist for New Tax Types\n1. [ ] **Schema**: Add `pro_id`, `dis_id`, and `sector_id` columns with proper types.\n2. [ ] **Import**: Implement \"Immediate ID Resolution\" in the PHP import script.\n3. [ ] **Import Report**: Show a summary of mapping successes/failures after upload.\n4. [ ] **UI Header**: Add \"Add Record\" and \"Run TE Calculation\" buttons.\n5. [ ] **Data Table**: Visually flag records with `NULL` IDs for user correction.\n6. [ ] **Modal**: Implement ID-based selects with dynamic chained filtering for districts.\n7. [ ] **Sync**: Ensure all code is synchronized to the XAMPP web root.\n",
